{"step_index":1924,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:38:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T09:38:59-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T09:38:59-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/aiSmsService.ts`\nTotal Lines: 151\nTotal Bytes: 8189\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import { Lead, CallLog, AppSettings } from '../types';\n2: import { SettingsRepository } from '../db/settingsRepository';\n3: import { CallLogsRepository } from '../db/callLogsRepository';\n4: \n5: export class AiSmsService {\n6:   /**\n7:    * Generates a clean, warm, friendly yet professional personalized SMS message for Florida educators.\n8:    * Draws directly from information on their scanned ValuTeachers report cards—particularly handwritten questions,\n9:    * notes, planning periods, room numbers, and retirement interests—aimed at setting a comfortable in-person classroom sit-down.\n10:    */\n11:   static async generatePersuasiveSMS(\n12:     lead: Lead,\n13:     currentDisposition?: string,\n14:     providedApiKey?: string,\n15:     toneFocus?: 'meeting_confirmation' | 'unanswered_followup' | 'drop_bonus_focus' | 'planning_period'\n16:   ): Promise<string> {\n17:     const settings = await SettingsRepository.getSettings();\n18:     const agentName = settings.user_name || 'Alex';\n19:     let key = providedApiKey || settings.gemini_api_key;\n20: \n21:     // If no API key, return a fully dynamic, complete tailored fallback\n22:     if (!key || key.trim().length === 0) {\n23:       return this.getSmartFallbackSMS(lead, agentName, toneFocus);\n24:     }\n25: \n26:     try {\n27:       const history = await CallLogsRepository.getLogsForLead(lead.id);\n28: \n29:       const historySummary = history\n30:         .slice(0, 3)\n31:         .map(\n32:           (h) =>\n33:             `- Outreach on ${new Date(h.timestamp).toLocaleDateString()}: \"${h.disposition}\"${\n34:               h.note ? ` (Note: ${h.note})` : ''\n35:             }`\n36:         )\n37:         .join('\\n');\n38: \n39:       const preferredTimes = (lead.meeting_preferences || []).join(', ') || '';\n40:       const interests = (lead.frs_interests || []).join(', ') || '';\n41:       const handwrittenQuestion = lead.custom_questions ? lead.custom_questions.trim() : '';\n42:       const agentNotes = lead.notes ? lead.notes.trim() : '';\n43: \n44:       const prompt = `\n45: You are a warm, professional, and consultative educational retirement advisor for ValuTeachers in Florida.\n46: You are writing a personalized SMS text message to a Florida public school teacher who filled out a handwritten ValuTeachers Report Card requesting an in-person planning session.\n47: \n48: EDUCATOR DETAILS (FROM SCANNED REPORT CARD):\n49: - Educator Name: ${lead.name}\n50: - School / Campus: ${lead.school || 'your school'}\n51: - Classroom / Room #: ${lead.room_number ? `Room ${lead.room_number}` : 'Classroom'}\n52: - Planning Period / Time: ${lead.planning_period || 'planning period'}\n53: - Years in Florida Retirement System (FRS): ${lead.years_in_frs ? `${lead.years_in_frs} years` : 'Not specified'}\n54: - FRS Knowledge Level: \"${lead.frs_knowledge || 'Moderate'}\"\n55: - Specific Needs / Topics Checked: ${interests || 'FRS Pension calculations, DROP, and 403(b) review'}\n56: - Handwritten Question / Note on Card: ${handwrittenQuestion ? `\"${handwrittenQuestion}\"` : 'None'}\n57: - Special File Notes: ${agentNotes ? `\"${agentNotes}\"` : 'None'}\n58: - Teacher's Requested Availability: ${preferredTimes || 'During planning period or after school'}\n59: - Call Status: ${currentDisposition || 'Outreach'}\n60: - Contact History:\n61: ${historySummary || 'First outreach.'}\n62: - ValuTeachers Representative Name: ${agentName}\n63: ${toneFocus ? `- Tone / Focus Preference: ${toneFocus.replace('_', ' ')}` : ''}\n64: \n65: WRITING OBJECTIVES & GUIDELINES:\n66: 1. Warm, Friendly & Professional: Write as an approachable local retirement specialist visiting their campus.\n67: 2. Address Their Handwritten Notes: If the teacher wrote a specific question or note on their card (\"${handwrittenQuestion}\"), ALWAYS acknowledge it directly (e.g., \"I saw your note asking about...\" or \"Regarding your question on...\").\n68: 3. Clear Goal: Invite them for a relaxed, 15-20 minute sit-down in their classroom during their planning period (${lead.planning_period || 'planning period'}) or preferred time (${preferredTimes || 'this week'}) to walk through their personalized FRS numbers.\n69: 4. Seamlessly incorporate relevant details: Mention their years in FRS (${lead.years_in_frs || 'service'}), DROP calculation, 5% bonus, or 403(b) clarity naturally without sounding like a robotic form letter.\n70: 5. NEVER Cut Off / Complete Thought: The message MUST be complete, grammatically sound, and end with an easy-to-answer closing question.\n71: 6. Length: Concise mobile length (around 2 to 4 sentences).\n72: 7. Format: Output ONLY the plain SMS text. Do NOT include quotation marks, markdown bolding, or intro/outro explanations.\n73: `;\n74: \n75:       const candidateModels = ['gemini-2.0-flash', 'gemini-1.5-flash', 'gemini-1.5-pro'];\n76: \n77:       for (const model of candidateModels) {\n78:         try {\n79:           const endpoint = `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/${model}:generateContent?key=${key}`;\n80: \n81:           const response = await fetch(endpoint, {\n82:             method: 'POST',\n83:             headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n84:             body: JSON.stringify({\n85:               contents: [{ parts: [{ text: prompt }] }],\n86:               generationConfig: {\n87:                 temperature: 0.35,\n88:                 maxOutputTokens: 600,\n89:               },\n90:             }),\n91:           });\n92: \n93:           if (response.ok) {\n94:             const data = await response.json();\n95:             const text = data?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text?.trim();\n96:             if (text && text.length > 20) {\n97:               return text.replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '').trim();\n98:             }\n99:           }\n100:         } catch {\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
